' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's own native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention.
'
' Real CALLABLE support: `ADDRESSOF Foo` and calling through a variable
' that holds one. A callable's own runtime identity is physically just a
' String naming its target function (reusing this backend's ordinary
' String representation verbatim), and a call through it dispatches via
' a real, closed, compile-time-enumerable candidate set (every ADDRESSOF
' target anywhere in the WHOLE MODULE, filtered by arity per call site)
' compared at runtime via `str_equals` -- the SAME real technique this
' backend's own polymorphic instance-method dispatch already uses for a
' `__class` tag, and the SAME real design the legacy native x86-64
' backend (src/compiler/fission.cpp, RFC-0049) already established for
' this exact feature. Only a plain function name is supported (a
' class-qualified or bound-instance-method ADDRESSOF target is real,
' disclosed, unattempted future work, matching the legacy backend's own
' identical restriction) -- not exercised here.
'
' Exercises: reassigning the SAME callable variable to different
' 1-argument targets; a 0-argument callable returning a String
' (disjoint-arity candidate set correctly does not interfere with a
' 1-argument callable elsewhere in the same module -- a real bug found
' and fixed this session, both for a call's own DEST kind and for
' argument-kind evidence feeding a callee whose ONLY real invocation is
' through a callable, never by its own name); a callable passed as an
' ordinary function PARAMETER and called from inside that function; a
' void call through a callable (no captured result) for both a
' 0-argument and a 1-argument target.
'
' Expected output verified against legacy `ArcoFission compile-run` on this
' identical source as the equivalence-testing oracle.
FUNCTION Square(x)
    RETURN x * x
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Double(x)
    RETURN x * 2
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Hello()
    RETURN "hi"
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION SayHi()
    PRINT "hi from SayHi"
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Greet(name)
    PRINT "hello " + name
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION ApplyTwice(fn, x)
    RETURN fn(fn(x))
END FUNCTION

f = ADDRESSOF Square
PRINT f(5)
f = ADDRESSOF Double
PRINT f(5)

g = ADDRESSOF Hello
PRINT g()

PRINT ApplyTwice(ADDRESSOF Double, 3)

h = ADDRESSOF SayHi
ignored = h()

k = ADDRESSOF Greet
ignored = k("world")
